  process with coffee  so when dispute arises let's say I  bought something and I claimed that I  didn't I never got it the merchant says  yeah you did get it and we are now we  now need arbitration so a committee of  these mediators will be randomly picked  they don't know each other they don't  discuss the case among each other and  now they need to vote if the merchant is  right or if the consumer is right but  they don't just do that as we need to  incentivize them because we are not  paying their salaries and we want to  encourage good usage of the network they  not only vote but they actually stake  some of their coins on either side so  pool is created and when it's time to  finalize the vote and and see who's  right there's a pool there of tokens and  the side that voted with the majority  actually splits the token between  themselves so the losing side loses  these tokens the winning side wins some  tokens so this is how you create this  delegated proof of  sake of sorts and you create this  mechanism that actually over time  encourages people to judge well because  if they don't judge well and they always  vote on the wrong side they'll actually  lose tokens and eventually leave this  game but people that actually judge well  or vote with the majority and actually  win more tokens overtime very very  interesting system that's one of the  elements I found most interesting in  learning about what you're doing we've  been working speaking with Shahab our  Geffen's CEO of cody you can learn more  about both the project and the token  sale by using the links in the video  description thank you so much for  talking to us about the project thank  you David  thank you very much

